          "Lines of Longitude (Meridians): Angular distance measured east or west of the Prime Meridian (Greenwich Meridian, 0°). All meridians run vertically from North Pole to South Pole and converge at the poles.",
          "Location of Ghana: Ghana lies entirely in the Northern and Western/Eastern hemispheres, between latitudes 4° 44' N and 11° 11' N, and between longitudes 1° 12' E and 3° 15' W.",
          "The Prime Meridian in Ghana: The Greenwich Meridian (0° Longitude) passes directly through the port city of Tema in the Greater Accra Region."
